Pick a floating workspace directory from the web client

In the tile, Settings > Floating Workspace > Terminal Directory's folder button
did nothing - no picker, no error - and no directory could be applied.

The desktop feature is three host operations the browser had a path for none of:
a native OS dialog, the trust grant that dialog also performs, and a cwd
resolution that only returns a custom path once it is trusted. Upstream's
`ipc/floating-workspace-directory.ts` already implements the last two, but pinned
them to Electron with two `app.getPath` calls, so the runtime graph could not
reach them - `config/runtime-electron-baseline.txt` is empty and must stay so.
Routing those two calls through `AppEnvironment`, the migration upstream already
performed on ~25 other modules, makes the module and its whole closure portable;
the helpers then narrow to the one settings field they read and write, so the
runtime passes its own store with no cast.

Two runtime methods, `floatingWorkspace.resolveCwd` and `grantDirectory`, reuse
those helpers; the web client opens the existing `RemoteFileBrowser`, then grants
over the runtime and stores what was picked. The grant goes through
`callRuntimeRpc`, following `runtime-server-directory-browser.ts`, rather than an
`AppApi` key the desktop would never call. Both methods mutate or authorize host
state, so neither is on `MOBILE_RPC_METHOD_ALLOWLIST`, and both resolve through
`requireStore()`: without persistence a grant is dropped while the call still
answers ok, so the pane would store a path `resolveCwd` then refuses. A refused
directory is not stored, because an ungranted path resolves to '' and the input
renders that as the configured path. The native dialog stays desktop-only.
Desktop changes once, deliberately:
`getFloatingWorkspaceDirectoryInputValue` returns the configured path while the
resolve is outstanding, or the field blanks visibly over a network hop.

To test, pick a directory in Settings > Floating Workspace in the tile, confirm
it is displayed back and check a floating terminal's cwd; then pick one the
server cannot grant and confirm the field does not change and the failure is
reported. The module must carry no `electron` import. Red with this patch popped:
`floating-workspace-directory-grant.test.ts` - the picker's three grant outcomes -
and `floating-workspace.test.ts`, the family's registration.
`FloatingWorkspacePane.test.tsx` and `floating-workspace-directory.test.ts` revert
to upstream's own versions and `mobile-rpc-allowlist.test.ts` is a patched file
whose cases popping deletes: all three stay green, so none of them is coverage.
